The artifacts this repository builds embed nothing. Both bundles declare every
product dependency at provided scope, neither carries a private package it does
not own, and no embedding, included-jar, or second class-path instruction
appears in either manifest. The check that decides this reads the produced
archives rather than the build configuration, so the claim above is a property
of the bytes this repository ships and not a statement about its intentions.

Because nothing is embedded, no third party's terms travel with these
artifacts, and this file names none. If that ever stops being true, the
imported-package footprint check fails before the artifact is published.
